{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Customer Reviews

  The band between the product page's proof bar and the footer: a rating summary
  (average, five-star row, 5→1 distribution bars, "write a review" CTA) over a
  grid of merchant-curated review cards, with the submission form in a modal
  dialog. Styled in assets/shudhi-reviews.css.

  There is no reviews app on this store. sections/sh-product.liquid:852-862
  carries a dormant Judge.me embed gated on `rating_real or
  product.metafields.judgeme.widget`, and neither is ever true today — so this
  section owns reviews on the PDP, and the reviews themselves are schema blocks.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  NINE THINGS HERE ARE LOAD-BEARING
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. THE ROOT CARRIES `sh`. assets/shudhi-home.js:300 selects `.sh [data-reveal]`
     and :331 selects `.sh [data-count-to]`. Without the bare class the CSS
     pre-state (shudhi-home.css:234) leaves every revealed element at opacity 0
     for the life of the page. Same rule as sh-faq.liquid note 2.

  2. [data-count-to] IS parseInt-ONLY. shudhi-home.js:356 reads the attribute
     with parseInt, so it animates the integer review COUNT and nothing else.
     The average is printed as static text — handing it "4.9" would count up to
     4 and land there. Both numbers ship as their real value in the markup, so
     they are correct with JS absent, blocked or still deferred.

  3. THE STAR IDS ARE SUFFIXED -{{ section.id }}. sh-product.liquid:184-185
     already defines `sh-star-…__main` and `sh-star-gold-…__main` on this same
     page. Two <defs> claiming one id is a silent collision — the second one
     loses and the gold gradient paints from the wrong stop set. The suffix is
     what keeps the two sections independent.

  4. THE AVERAGE AND THE BARS ARE COUNTED, NOT TYPED. One pass below tallies the
     live blocks, sums the ratings and buckets the distribution. A merchant
     cannot enter a headline number that disagrees with the reviews underneath
     it. (The star row inside sh-product.liquid is a separate, hand-typed
     setting — see the schema note on `count_note`.)

  5. {% form 'contact' %} TAKES NO CUSTOM id:. Shopify sets id="contact_form"
     itself; passing one breaks the anchor it redirects to. And form.* is only
     readable INSIDE the form block — computing it outside evaluates against nil,
     the exact bug sh-contact.liquid:141-165 documents having already fixed once.

  6. OVERFLOW CARDS ARE HIDDEN BY JS, NOT BY LIQUID. Every review renders
     visible; assets/sh-reviews.js adds [hidden] past `initial_count` on boot.
     Reversing that would hide reviews from crawlers and from anyone whose JS
     never arrives — the list must fail open, the same way the reveal does.

  7. THE JSON-LD SELF-SUPPRESSES. layout/theme.liquid:28-73 owns the Product
     node and deliberately emits aggregateRating ONLY from the reviews.*
     metafields. This block is off by default and additionally refuses to render
     whenever that metafield exists, so the page can never carry two conflicting
     aggregate ratings.

  8. THE HEADLINE AND THE LIST SHARE ONE SOURCE. Judge.me writes Shopify's
     standard reviews.rating / reviews.rating_count metafields, but those are
     read ONLY in shell mode — where the app also renders the list underneath.
     Reading them in manual mode produced exactly the contradiction you would
     expect: a "Based on 1 review" headline from the app sitting above two
     hand-entered cards. Whoever supplies the number supplies the reviews.

  9. AN @app BLOCK SWITCHES THIS INTO A SHELL. Drop the Judge.me Review Widget
     block inside this section and it takes over the list, the histogram and the
     write-a-review flow — so the band's own bars, CTA, cards, load-more, dialog
     and JSON-LD all stand down rather than compete with it. What is left is the
     part worth keeping: the cream band, the serif heading and the headline
     rating. `{% render block %}` is the supported way to host an app block; it
     is what keeps this working when Judge.me changes their markup.

  The review body is a textarea rendered through `newline_to_br` + `escape`, not
  richtext: a review is someone else's words and should not carry markup a
  merchant can style into a marketing claim.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'shudhi-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}
{%- assign uid = section.id | default: 'rev' -%}

{%- comment -%} See (4). One pass: count, sum, bucket. Also counts app blocks,
    because their presence is what switches this section into "shell" mode. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign app_blocks = 0 -%}
{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}{%- assign app_blocks = app_blocks | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} Shell mode: an app block owns the list and the submit flow, so
    this section contributes the band, the heading and the headline number only. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign shell = false -%}
{%- if app_blocks > 0 -%}{%- assign shell = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- assign live = 0 -%}
{%- assign total = 0 -%}
{%- assign c5 = 0 -%}
{%- assign c4 = 0 -%}
{%- assign c3 = 0 -%}
{%- assign c2 = 0 -%}
{%- assign c1 = 0 -%}
{%- for block in section.blocks -%}
  {%- if block.settings.author == blank or block.settings.body == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- assign live = live | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- assign r = block.settings.rating | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- assign total = total | plus: r -%}
  {%- case r -%}
    {%- when 5 -%}{%- assign c5 = c5 | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- when 4 -%}{%- assign c4 = c4 | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign c3 = c3 | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign c2 = c2 | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- else -%}{%- assign c1 = c1 | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if live > 0 -%}
  {%- assign avg = total | times: 1.0 | divided_by: live -%}
  {%- assign avg_txt = avg | round: 1 -%}
  {%- assign avg_pct = avg | divided_by: 5.0 | times: 100 | round: 2 -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} See (8). Judge.me writes Shopify's standard reviews.* metafields,
    so when the app is live the headline number comes from real, moderated data
    and the manual blocks stop being the source. Identical resolution order to
    sections/sh-product.liquid:105-118, so the two can never disagree. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rv = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value -%}
{%- assign rc = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | plus: 0 -%}
{%- assign rating_real = false -%}
{%- if shell and rv.rating != blank and rc > 0 -%}
  {%- assign rating_real = true -%}
  {%- assign rmax = rv.scale_max | default: 5 | times: 1.0 -%}
  {%- assign avg = rv.rating | times: 1.0 -%}
  {%- assign avg_txt = avg | round: 1 -%}
  {%- assign avg_pct = avg | divided_by: rmax | times: 100 | round: 2 -%}
  {%- assign live = rc -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign has_content = false -%}
{%- if live > 0 or shell -%}{%- assign has_content = true -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- if has_content -%}
<section class="sh sh-rev{% if shell %} sh-rev--shell{% endif %}"
         id="sh-reviews"
         style="--sh-rev-bg:{{ s.bg }};--sh-rev-pad-top:{{ s.pad_top }}px;--sh-rev-pad-bottom:{{ s.pad_bottom }}px;"
         data-sh-rev
         data-rev-initial="{{ s.initial_count }}"
         aria-labelledby="sh-rev-title-{{ uid }}">
  <div class="sh-wrap">

    {%- comment -%} See (3). A zero-size svg, so where it sits in the flow is free. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture star_row -%}
      <use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" x="0" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" x="24" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" x="48" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" x="72" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" x="96" width="20" height="20"/>
    {%- endcapture -%}
    <svg class="sh-rev__defs" width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <defs>
        <symbol id="sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" viewBox="0 0 22 20" overflow="visible"><path d="M10.525.464a.5.5 0 0 1 .95 0l2.107 6.482a.5.5 0 0 0 .475.346h6.817a.5.5 0 0 1 .294.904l-5.515 4.007a.5.5 0 0 0-.181.559l2.106 6.483a.5.5 0 0 1-.77.559l-5.514-4.007a.5.5 0 0 0-.588 0l-5.514 4.007a.5.5 0 0 1-.77-.56l2.106-6.482a.5.5 0 0 0-.181-.56L.832 8.197a.5.5 0 0 1 .294-.904h6.817a.5.5 0 0 0 .475-.346z"/></symbol>
        <linearGradient id="sh-rev-gold-{{ uid }}" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#ac8940"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#7a5d2e"/></linearGradient>
      </defs>
    </svg>

    <header class="sh-rev__head"{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %}>
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="sh-rev__eyebrow sh-eyebrow">
          {{ s.eyebrow }}{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h2 class="sh-rev__title sh-serif" id="sh-rev-title-{{ uid }}">
        {{- s.title | default: 'Customer Reviews' -}}
      </h2>
      {%- if s.body != blank -%}
        <p class="sh-rev__lede">{{ s.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    {%- if s.show_summary -%}
      <div class="sh-rev__summary"{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %}>

        <div class="sh-rev__score">
          {%- comment -%} See (2): the average is text, only the count animates. {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="sh-rev__avg sh-serif" aria-hidden="true">{{ avg_txt }}</p>
          <span class="sh-rev__stars" role="img" aria-label="Rated {{ avg_txt }} out of 5 from {{ live }} {% if live == 1 %}review{% else %}reviews{% endif %}" style="--sh-rating:{{ avg_pct }}%">
            <span class="sh-rev__stars-base" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="sh-rev__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg>
            </span>
            <span class="sh-rev__stars-fill" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg class="sh-rev__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="url(#sh-rev-gold-{{ uid }})" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg>
            </span>
          </span>
          <p class="sh-rev__based" aria-hidden="true">
            Based on <span data-count-to="{{ live }}">{{ live }}</span> {% if live == 1 %}review{% else %}reviews{% endif %}
          </p>
        </div>

        {%- if s.show_bars and shell == false -%}
          {%- comment -%} A table would claim tabular semantics for what is a
              summary; a plain list with a visually-hidden sentence per row keeps
              it readable to a screen reader without the grid overhead. {%- endcomment -%}
          <ul class="sh-rev__bars" aria-label="Rating breakdown">
            {%- for tier in (1..5) -%}
              {%- assign star = 6 | minus: tier -%}
              {%- case star -%}
                {%- when 5 -%}{%- assign n = c5 -%}
                {%- when 4 -%}{%- assign n = c4 -%}
                {%- when 3 -%}{%- assign n = c3 -%}
                {%- when 2 -%}{%- assign n = c2 -%}
                {%- else -%}{%- assign n = c1 -%}
              {%- endcase -%}
              {%- assign pct = n | times: 100.0 | divided_by: live | round: 2 -%}
              <li class="sh-rev__bar-row">
                <span class="sh-rev__bar-label" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="sh-rev__bar-n">{{ star }}</span>
                  <svg class="sh-rev__bar-star" viewBox="0 0 22 20" fill="url(#sh-rev-gold-{{ uid }})" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" width="22" height="20"/></svg>
                </span>
                <span class="sh-rev__bar-track" aria-hidden="true">
                  <span class="sh-rev__bar-fill" style="--w:{{ pct }}%"></span>
                </span>
                <span class="sh-rev__bar-count" aria-hidden="true">{{ n }}</span>
                <span class="sh-visually-hidden">{{ star }} stars: {{ n }} of {{ live }}</span>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.enable_form and shell == false -%}
          <div class="sh-rev__cta">
            {%- if s.cta_note != blank -%}<p class="sh-rev__cta-note">{{ s.cta_note }}</p>{%- endif -%}
            <button type="button" class="sh-rev__open" data-rev-open aria-haspopup="dialog">
              {{ s.cta_label | default: 'Write a review' }}
            </button>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%} See (9). The app owns the list in shell mode; the hand-entered
        cards below are the fallback for a store with no reviews app. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if shell -%}
      <div class="sh-rev__app">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}
            <div class="sh-rev__app-block" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{% render block %}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- else -%}

    {%- comment -%} See (6). Every card renders visible; the JS hides the tail. {%- endcomment -%}
    <ul class="sh-rev__list" data-rev-list>
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.settings.author == blank or block.settings.body == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign r = block.settings.rating | plus: 0 -%}
        {%- assign r_pct = r | times: 20 -%}
        {%- assign initial = block.settings.author | strip | slice: 0 | upcase -%}
        <li class="sh-rev__card" data-rev-card{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %} {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>

          <div class="sh-rev__card-top">
            <span class="sh-rev__avatar" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- if block.settings.avatar != blank -%}
                <img src="{{ block.settings.avatar | image_url: width: 96 }}" width="40" height="40" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="sh-rev__initial">{{ initial }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>

            <div class="sh-rev__who">
              <p class="sh-rev__name">
                {{ block.settings.author }}
                {%- if block.settings.verified -%}
                  <span class="sh-rev__verified">
                    {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'badge', sw: 1.6 %}
                    <span>Verified</span>
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>
              <span class="sh-rev__stars sh-rev__stars--sm" role="img" aria-label="Rated {{ r }} out of 5" style="--sh-rating:{{ r_pct }}%">
                <span class="sh-rev__stars-base" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg class="sh-rev__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg>
                </span>
                <span class="sh-rev__stars-fill" aria-hidden="true">
                  <svg class="sh-rev__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="url(#sh-rev-gold-{{ uid }})" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg>
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>

            {%- if block.settings.date != blank -%}
              <span class="sh-rev__date">{{ block.settings.date }}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>

          {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
            <h3 class="sh-rev__card-title">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
          {%- endif -%}

          <p class="sh-rev__body">{{ block.settings.body | escape | newline_to_br }}</p>

          {%- assign block_photo = block.settings.photo -%}
          {%- if block_photo != blank -%}
            {%- comment -%} A customer's own photo of the product. Fixed intrinsic
                dimensions and lazy/async because it sits below the fold on every
                breakpoint — it must never become the LCP candidate. {%- endcomment -%}
            <a class="sh-rev__photo" href="{{ block_photo | image_url: width: 1400 }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <img src="{{ block_photo | image_url: width: 320 }}"
                   srcset="{{ block_photo | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w,
                           {{ block_photo | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w"
                   sizes="120px"
                   width="120" height="120"
                   alt="Photo from {{ block.settings.author | escape }}'s review"
                   loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {%- comment -%} Rendered hidden and revealed by the JS only when there is
        actually a tail to reveal, so it never sits there doing nothing. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sh-rev__more-wrap">
      <button type="button" class="sh-rev__more" data-rev-more hidden>
        {{ s.more_label | default: 'Load more reviews' }}
      </button>
    </div>

    {%- endif -%}{%- comment -%} end manual-mode list {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- if s.enable_form and shell == false -%}
      {%- comment -%} See (5). Shopify redirects back here with
          ?contact_posted=true, so the dialog has to be able to reopen itself on
          that load to show the confirmation — hence data-rev-open-on-load. {%- endcomment -%}
      <dialog class="sh-rev__dialog" data-rev-dialog aria-labelledby="sh-rev-form-title-{{ uid }}">
        <div class="sh-rev__dialog-in">

          <button type="button" class="sh-rev__close" data-rev-close aria-label="Close">
            {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'close', sw: 1.6 %}
          </button>

          {%- form 'contact', class: 'sh-form sh-rev__form' -%}
            {%- assign posted = false -%}
            {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}{%- assign posted = true -%}{%- endif -%}

            {%- if posted or form.errors -%}
              <span data-rev-open-on-load hidden></span>
            {%- endif -%}

            <div class="sh-form__inner">
              {%- if posted -%}
                <h2 class="sh-rev__form-title sh-serif" id="sh-rev-form-title-{{ uid }}" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
                  {{ s.success_title | default: 'Thank you' }}
                </h2>
                <p class="sh-form__ok">
                  {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}
                  <span>{{ s.success_text }}</span>
                </p>
              {%- else -%}
                <h2 class="sh-rev__form-title sh-serif" id="sh-rev-form-title-{{ uid }}">
                  {{ s.form_title | default: 'Write a review' }}
                </h2>

                {%- if form.errors -%}
                  <div class="sh-form__err" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
                    {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'alert' %}
                    <div>
                      <p class="sh-form__err-title">Please check the highlighted fields.</p>
                      {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                {%- elsif s.form_lede != blank -%}
                  <p class="sh-form__lede">{{ s.form_lede }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}

                <div class="sh-form__body">

                  {%- comment -%} Reversed on purpose: the radios run 5→1 in the
                      DOM and the row is row-reverse in CSS, so `:checked ~ label`
                      paints the star itself plus every LOWER one with no JS. {%- endcomment -%}
                  <fieldset class="sh-rev__rate">
                    <legend class="sh-field__label">
                      Your rating<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                    </legend>
                    <div class="sh-rev__rate-row">
                      {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                        {%- assign v = 6 | minus: i -%}
                        <input class="sh-rev__rate-in" type="radio" id="sh-rev-r{{ v }}-{{ uid }}"
                               name="contact[rating]" value="{{ v }} out of 5"
                               required aria-required="true">
                        <label class="sh-rev__rate-label" for="sh-rev-r{{ v }}-{{ uid }}">
                          <svg viewBox="0 0 22 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#sh-rev-star-{{ uid }}" width="22" height="20"/></svg>
                          <span class="sh-visually-hidden">{{ v }} {% if v == 1 %}star{% else %}stars{% endif %}</span>
                        </label>
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </div>
                  </fieldset>

                  <div class="sh-form__row">
                    <div class="sh-field">
                      <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-rev-name-{{ uid }}">
                        Your name<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                      </label>
                      <input type="text" id="sh-rev-name-{{ uid }}" name="contact[name]"
                             required aria-required="true" autocomplete="name"
                             value="{{ form.name | default: customer.name }}">
                    </div>
                    <div class="sh-field">
                      <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-rev-email-{{ uid }}">
                        Email<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                      </label>
                      <input type="email" id="sh-rev-email-{{ uid }}" name="contact[email]"
                             required aria-required="true" autocomplete="email"
                             aria-describedby="sh-rev-email-hint-{{ uid }}"
                             value="{{ form.email | default: customer.email }}">
                      <p class="sh-field__hint" id="sh-rev-email-hint-{{ uid }}">Not published — we only use it to verify your order.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="sh-field">
                    <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-rev-title-in-{{ uid }}">Review title</label>
                    <input type="text" id="sh-rev-title-in-{{ uid }}" name="contact[review_title]" maxlength="80">
                  </div>

                  <div class="sh-field">
                    <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-rev-body-{{ uid }}">
                      Your review<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                    </label>
                    <textarea id="sh-rev-body-{{ uid }}" name="contact[body]" rows="5"
                              required aria-required="true">{{ form.body }}</textarea>
                  </div>

                  {%- if product != blank -%}
                    <input type="hidden" name="contact[product]" value="{{ product.title | escape }}">
                    <input type="hidden" name="contact[product_url]" value="{{ shop.url }}{{ product.url }}">
                  {%- endif -%}

                  <div class="sh-form__actions">
                    <button type="submit" class="sh-rev__submit">
                      {{ s.submit_label | default: 'Submit review' }}
                    </button>
                  </div>

                  {%- if s.form_note != blank -%}
                    <p class="sh-form__privacy">{{ s.form_note }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}

                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endform -%}

        </div>
      </dialog>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} See (7). Off by default, and refused outright whenever the real
    metafield exists so layout/theme.liquid stays the single source of the
    aggregate rating. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if s.enable_jsonld and shell == false and product != blank and product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating == blank -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org/",
    "@type": "Product",
    "@id": {{ canonical_url | append: '#product' | json }},
    "name": {{ product.title | json }},
    "url": {{ canonical_url | json }},
    "aggregateRating": {
      "@type": "AggregateRating",
      "ratingValue": {{ avg_txt | json }},
      "bestRating": "5",
      "worstRating": "1",
      "reviewCount": {{ live | json }}
    },
    "review": [
      {%- assign j = 0 -%}
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- if block.settings.author == blank or block.settings.body == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- assign j = j | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- if j > 1 %},{% endif %}
        {
          "@type": "Review",
          "reviewRating": {
            "@type": "Rating",
            "ratingValue": {{ block.settings.rating | plus: 0 | json }},
            "bestRating": "5",
            "worstRating": "1"
          },
          "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": {{ block.settings.author | json }} },
          {%- if block.settings.title != blank %}
          "name": {{ block.settings.title | json }},
          {%- endif %}
          "reviewBody": {{ block.settings.body | json }}
        }
      {%- endfor -%}
    ]
  }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Liquid has no and/or precedence — it folds right to left — so this
    stays a single condition. Both jobs the script does (load-more, dialog) exist
    only in manual mode, which makes `shell == false` the whole test. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if shell == false -%}
  <script src="{{ 'sh-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Customer Reviews",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Reviews are entered here as blocks. The average, the star row and the breakdown bars are all calculated from them — there is no number to keep in sync." },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The reviews this section ships with are SAMPLES. Replace every one with a genuine customer review before you publish." },

    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "In their words" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Customer Reviews" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Supporting line", "default": "Read what the Shudhi Ritual™ has meant for people who use it every day." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Summary" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_summary", "label": "Show the rating summary", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_bars", "label": "Show the 5→1 breakdown bars", "default": true },

    { "type": "header", "content": "List" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "initial_count", "label": "Reviews shown before “Load more”", "min": 2, "max": 24, "step": 1, "default": 6,
      "info": "The rest stay in the page and are revealed by the button. If a visitor has JavaScript turned off they simply see all of them at once." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "more_label", "label": "Load-more button text", "default": "Load more reviews" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Write a review" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_form", "label": "Let customers submit a review", "default": true,
      "info": "Submissions are emailed to the store contact address — they do NOT publish themselves. Add the ones you want to show as blocks below." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_note", "label": "Small label above the button", "default": "Used the bar?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button text", "default": "Write a review" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "form_title", "label": "Form heading", "default": "Write a review" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "form_lede", "label": "Form intro", "default": "Tell us how the ritual has been for you. We read every note that comes in." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "submit_label", "label": "Submit button text", "default": "Submit review" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "form_note", "label": "Small print under the form", "default": "Your email is never published. Reviews are checked before they appear here." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_title", "label": "Confirmation heading", "default": "Thank you" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "success_text", "label": "Confirmation message", "default": "Your review is with us. We read every one, and yours may appear on this page shortly." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Search results" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "enable_jsonld", "label": "Publish these reviews as search-results markup", "default": false,
      "info": "Leave OFF until every review here is a genuine customer submission. Publishing invented reviews as structured data breaks Google's review policy and risks a manual penalty on the whole domain. It also switches itself off automatically if a reviews app is ever installed." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#e9e0cf",
      "info": "A half-step deeper than the product page above it, so the band reads as its own beat before the green footer. Keep it light — the text colours are tuned for a light surface." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pad_top", "label": "Top padding", "min": 0, "max": 140, "step": 4, "default": 72, "unit": "px" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pad_bottom", "label": "Bottom padding", "min": 0, "max": 140, "step": 4, "default": 88, "unit": "px" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@app" },
    { "type": "review", "name": "Review", "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "rating", "label": "Rating", "default": "5",
        "options": [
          { "value": "5", "label": "5 stars" },
          { "value": "4", "label": "4 stars" },
          { "value": "3", "label": "3 stars" },
          { "value": "2", "label": "2 stars" },
          { "value": "1", "label": "1 star" }
        ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "author", "label": "Name", "default": "Customer name",
        "info": "Required — a review with no name or no text is skipped entirely." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "date", "label": "Date", "default": "—",
        "info": "Free text, shown exactly as you type it. Clear it to hide the date entirely." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Review title" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Review", "default": "Replace this with a genuine customer review." },
      { "type": "checkbox", "id": "verified", "label": "Show the “Verified” badge", "default": true,
        "info": "Only tick this where you can actually match the review to an order." },
      { "type": "image_picker", "id": "avatar", "label": "Reviewer’s photo",
        "info": "Optional — the small round portrait next to the name. Falls back to the first letter of the name." },
      { "type": "image_picker", "id": "photo", "label": "Photo with the review",
        "info": "Optional — a customer’s own photo of the product, shown as a thumbnail under the review text. Click opens it full size." }
    ] }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 50,
  "presets": [ { "name": "SH · Customer Reviews", "blocks": [
    { "type": "review", "settings": { "rating": "5", "author": "Customer name", "title": "Sample review — replace me", "body": "Replace this with a genuine customer review before publishing. The average, the star row and the breakdown bars are all calculated from these blocks.", "verified": false } },
    { "type": "review", "settings": { "rating": "5", "author": "Customer name", "title": "Sample review — replace me", "body": "Replace this with a genuine customer review before publishing.", "verified": false } },
    { "type": "review", "settings": { "rating": "4", "author": "Customer name", "title": "Sample review — replace me", "body": "Replace this with a genuine customer review before publishing.", "verified": false } }
  ] } ]
}
{% endschema %}
